Frame cap fix, dxgi.maxFrameLatency override and DXMT_STATS_FILE

- d3d11.preferredMaxFrameRate is now only a lower bound on frame time.
  Before, SyncInterval was divided by the cap instead of the refresh rate,
  so a game presenting with SyncInterval=2 at cap 60 got 30 FPS.
- dxgi.maxFrameLatency=N fixes the CPU/GPU frame latency (PresentBoundary)
  and ignores the game's SetMaximumFrameLatency. 0 (default) keeps it.
- DXMT_STATS_FILE=<windows path> appends one line per 2 s with frame time
  percentiles and DXMT's per-frame stats. Used by scripts/bench-game.sh.

